      "updated_at": "2024-03-16T02:44:08Z",
      "body": "Another thought - the issue could be with the CI action itself. The CIFuzz job uses the `master` branch of the actions, so CPython's CI results are going to be dependent on the stability of the upstream repo. \r\n\r\nAs an experiment, I modified the CIFuzz checkout on an older version of the action, and [ran it on a copy of #116454](https://github.com/freakboy3742/cpython/pull/4). \r\n\r\nIf I revert to the 10e6cbd7 commit to oss-fuzz from a couple of days ago, the [CIFuzz test fails because of a clang issue failing to compile the code](https://github.com/freakboy3742/cpython/actions/runs/8304625844/job/22730491004), which is at least a *different* failure, and demonstrates that there's at least *some* sensitivity to the oss-fuzz version. \r\n",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
